       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify going above that. At that dose, the risks of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects go up, and there is little evidence of added benefit.\n\nPlease check these before we go further:\n- **Typo or unit error:** Did you mean 40 mg, or 200 mg?\n- **Usual dosing:** The usual start is 25\u201350 mg daily. Titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week, up to 200 mg/day.\n- **Indication:** Check the target dose for the condition. For example, OCD and depression often need higher doses within the 50\u2013200 mg range.\n- **Interacting drugs:** Check for other serotonergic agents, QT-prolonging drugs, anticoagulants, and NSAIDs.\n\nIf a higher dose is truly intended, for example by a psychiatry recommendation, talk to your resident or attending and pharmacy first. Then tell me, and I can enter it with a note documenting the approval.\n\nIf you tell me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 200 mg PO once daily, I'll enter it right away."
      }
